Tam,

csvToUMF requires very specific column names to work (which is a little unclear in the documentation). If you rename your obs.1-obs.27 columns to y.1-y.27 instead and rename "location" to "site", it should import correctly:

library(unmarked)
library(stringr)

inp <- read.csv('trialds2.csv')
names(inp) <- str_replace(names(inp),'obs','y')
names(inp)[1] <- 'site'
write.csv(inp,file='trialds2_new.csv',row.names=F)

test <- csvToUMF('trialds2_new.csv',type='unmarkedFrameOccu')

Ken

